diff --git a/ideaspark_run/world-action-model-quantization/phase4/derive_map.json b/ideaspark_run/world-action-model-quantization/phase4/derive_map.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5826aace9d0a934de8683a426922fc606618f92c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ideaspark_run/world-action-model-quantization/phase4/derive_map.json
@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@
+{
+  "title_zh": "量化 World Action Models 的因果后果校准",
+  "plain_motivation_en": "For a coupled future-video/action World Action Model (WAM), post-training quantization (PTQ) calibration is not only about reproducing local tensor values. A numerical intervention can change the predicted full action chunk; after the first action is executed, it can also change the simulator's next observation. The practical bottleneck is deciding which weight/activation (W/A) sites should stay at high precision when a local PTQ discrepancy does not consistently identify contact-transition consequences. OTC-PTQ therefore treats the full action chunk as an intermediate object and the one resulting control transition as the measurable boundary.\n\nThe current Phase 0 frontier makes this boundary testable. QuantWAMs (arxiv:2607.28405v1) makes joint video/action sensitivity and closed-loop protection explicit, QuantWM (arxiv:2602.02110v1) provides a distinct latent rollout/planning sensitivity branch, and Fast-WAM provides the named `idm` feasibility path without providing a numerical PTQ consequence signal. Together with the stated RoboTwin 2.0/LIBERO manipulation split and Fast-WAM-only staged validation budget, this supports a small one-transition diagnostic, provided the exact Optional IDM checkpoint identity is fixed in the pre-run manifest.\n\nSeveral adjacent directions are already covered. QuantWAMs measures joint video/action sensitivity and repairs closed-loop protection schedules; QuantWM studies weight/activation PTQ sensitivity and long-horizon latent planning; and Fast-WAM does not provide a numerical PTQ consequence signal for one-site W/A protection allocation. Earlier task-consequence work—VAML, Model Advantage / Value-Aware Model Learning, and Deep Task-Based Quantization—already shows that downstream consequence can guide targeting, while SQIL covers critical-state protection through saliency-weighted QAT and action distillation. The narrower gap is whether one numerical W/A intervention, with every other target site at FP16, can provide a reproducible one-control-transition proxy from paired full-action-chunk and next-observation discrepancy. OTC-PTQ does not claim those broader downstream-consequence or critical-state-targeting principles as new.\n\nIf this gap closes, the field gains a bounded diagnostic for identifying when local PTQ discrepancy stops predicting one-control-transition consequence on contact states. It complements QuantWAMs' closed-loop protection branch and QuantWM's latent-planning sensitivity branch. It also enables a test of whether a `C_r`-ranked schedule transfers to held-out contact-sensitive failures and next-observation deviation under the same precision budget, with permutation separating the consequence association from quantizer and site-count controls. This would not establish task-loss identity, a full-horizon/replan marginal, joint-low-bit optimality, or a bytes/latency objective.",
+  "plain_motivation_zh": "对于一个耦合 future-video/action 的 World Action Model（WAM），post-training quantization（PTQ）校准不只是复现局部 tensor 数值。一次 numerical intervention 可能改变模型预测的完整 action chunk；只执行第一个 action 后，simulator 的 next observation 也可能改变。实际瓶颈是选择哪些 weight/activation（W/A）site 保持 high precision，因为 local PTQ discrepancy 并不能稳定识别 contact-transition states 上的 consequence。因此，OTC-PTQ 把完整 action chunk 当作中间对象，把随后产生的一次 control transition 作为可测量边界。\n\n当前 Phase 0 frontier 使这个边界可以被测试。QuantWAMs（arxiv:2607.28405v1）明确处理 joint video/action sensitivity 和 closed-loop protection，QuantWM（arxiv:2602.02110v1）提供不同的 latent rollout/planning sensitivity 分支，Fast-WAM 则提供名为 `idm` 的 feasibility path，但没有提供 numerical PTQ consequence signal。结合已经说明的 RoboTwin 2.0/LIBERO manipulation split 和 Fast-WAM-only staged validation budget，现在可以进行一个小规模 one-transition diagnostic；前提是 pre-run manifest 中固定 exact Optional IDM checkpoint identity。\n\n几个相邻方向已经有工作覆盖。QuantWAMs 测量 joint video/action sensitivity，并修复 closed-loop protection schedule；QuantWM 研究 weight/activation PTQ sensitivity 和 long-horizon latent planning；Fast-WAM 没有提供用于 one-site W/A protection allocation 的 numerical PTQ consequence signal。更早的 task-consequence 工作——VAML、Model Advantage / Value-Aware Model Learning 和 Deep Task-Based Quantization——已经说明 downstream consequence 可以指导 targeting；SQIL 则通过 saliency-weighted QAT 和 action distillation 覆盖 critical-state protection。因此，更窄的 gap 是：当其他 target site 全部保持 FP16 时，一次 numerical W/A intervention 能否根据 paired full-action-chunk 和 next-observation discrepancy，提供可复现的 one-control-transition proxy。OTC-PTQ 不把这些更广泛的 downstream-consequence 或 critical-state-targeting 原则宣称为新贡献。\n\n如果这个 gap 被填补，领域将得到一个有界 diagnostic，用来识别 local PTQ discrepancy 何时不再预测 contact states 上的一次 control transition consequence。它补充 QuantWAMs 的 closed-loop protection 分支和 QuantWM 的 latent-planning sensitivity 分支。它还可以检验 `C_r`-ranked schedule 是否能在相同 precision budget 下迁移到 held-out contact-sensitive failures 和 next-observation deviation；permutation 可以把 consequence association 与 quantizer 和 site-count controls 区分开来。这不会证明 task-loss identity、full-horizon/replan marginal、joint-low-bit optimality 或 bytes/latency objective。",
+  "plain_method_steps_en": [
+    {
+      "step_id": "S1",
+      "what_to_do": "Before any paired measurement, freeze the calibration registry and pre-run manifest, including the exact Fast-WAM checkpoint identity and the `idm` configuration. Make controller, RNG, history, and cache restoration executable so the calibration state can be replayed. For the Optional IDM path, halt if the exact checkpoint identity is absent or mismatched.",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "Both branches are interpretable as a paired consequence only when they start from the same recoverable state. This preserves the version boundary instead of treating an unverified checkpoint as interchangeable."
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S2",
+      "what_to_do": "For each numerical weight or activation site r, apply the chosen low-bit operator only at r and keep every other target site at FP16. Produce the single-site low-bit branch paired with the FP16 reference for the same calibration record.",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "This isolates the bounded single-site intervention and avoids treating joint coupling, joint-low-bit marginal effects, or joint optimality as new claims."
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S3",
+      "what_to_do": "Run both branches to produce the full action chunk. From the restored state, execute only the first action and record the next observation. Compute `C_r` from normalized full-action-chunk MSE plus next-observation pixel L1, alongside the local score.",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "This defines a one-control-transition proxy for action-mediated consequence. `C_r` is not task loss, a full-horizon/replan marginal, or a jointly-low-bit marginal."
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S4",
+      "what_to_do": "Rank sites separately by `C_r` and by local discrepancy, then form protection schedules under the same high-precision-unit budget `B` and the declared site count `B_site`. Keep site count separate from bytes and latency.",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "The comparison tests whether the proxy changes protection choices at a matched precision budget, rather than introducing a storage or runtime objective."
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S5",
+      "what_to_do": "On the exact manifest, run `idm` with `sigma_shift_FW=1.0` and `infer_action` on the stated small held-out RoboTwin 2.0/LIBERO manipulation split, using the same `b_lo` and `B`. Compare contact-sensitive task failures and next-observation deviation for the two schedules. Then permute `C_r` across the site registry and use the stated oracle simulator-state branch as a positive control.",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "The contact-transition subset and permutation are mechanism tests: the candidate predicts ranking divergence and transfer for the real `C_r` association, with the advantage disappearing after permutation. The oracle branch checks calibration noise."
+    }
+  ],
+  "plain_method_steps_zh": [
+    {
+      "step_id": "S1",
+      "what_to_do": "在任何 paired measurement 之前，冻结 calibration registry 和 pre-run manifest，其中包括 exact Fast-WAM checkpoint identity 与 `idm` configuration。让 controller、RNG、history 和 cache restoration 可以执行，从而能够 replay calibration state。对于 Optional IDM path，如果 exact checkpoint identity 缺失或不匹配，就 halt。",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "只有两个 branch 都从同一个可恢复 state 开始，paired consequence 才能解释。这样可以保留 version boundary，不会把未经验证的 checkpoint 当作可互换对象。"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S2",
+      "what_to_do": "对每个 numerical weight 或 activation site r，只在 r 应用选定的 low-bit operator，其余 target site 全部保持 FP16。针对同一条 calibration record，生成与 FP16 reference 配对的 single-site low-bit branch。",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "这会隔离有界的 single-site intervention，也避免把 joint coupling、joint-low-bit marginal effects 或 joint optimality 当作新的 claim。"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S3",
+      "what_to_do": "运行两个 branch，生成完整 action chunk。从 restored state 出发，只执行第一个 action，并记录 next observation。用 normalized full-action-chunk MSE 加上 next-observation pixel L1 计算 `C_r`，同时保留 local score。",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "这定义了一个表示 action-mediated consequence 的 one-control-transition proxy。`C_r` 不是 task loss、full-horizon/replan marginal，也不是 jointly-low-bit marginal。"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S4",
+      "what_to_do": "分别按照 `C_r` 和 local discrepancy 对 site 排名，然后在相同的 high-precision-unit budget `B` 和声明的 site count `B_site` 下形成 protection schedule。把 site count 与 bytes、latency 分开。",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "这个比较检验 proxy 是否会在匹配的 precision budget 下改变 protection choice，而不是引入 storage 或 runtime objective。"
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S5",
+      "what_to_do": "在 exact manifest 上，使用 `sigma_shift_FW=1.0` 运行 `idm`，并在指定的小规模 held-out RoboTwin 2.0/LIBERO manipulation split 上运行 `infer_action`；两者使用相同的 `b_lo` 和 `B`。比较两个 schedule 的 contact-sensitive task failures 与 next-observation deviation。随后在 site registry 中 permutation `C_r`，并使用指定的 oracle simulator-state branch 作为 positive control。",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "contact-transition subset 和 permutation 是 mechanism tests：candidate 预测真实 `C_r` association 会带来 ranking divergence 和 transfer，而 permutation 后这个 advantage 会消失。oracle branch 用来检查 calibration noise。"
+    }
+  ],
+  "plain_method_modules_en": [
+    {
+      "module_id": "M1_background",
+      "purpose_oneline": "Provide replayable calibration states and exact version and configuration boundaries for paired measurement.",
+      "step_ids": ["S1"]
+    },
+    {
+      "module_id": "M2_one_transition_proxy",
+      "purpose_oneline": "Create the bounded single-site W/A intervention and compute the one-control-transition `C_r` signal.",
+      "step_ids": ["S2", "S3"]
+    },
+    {
+      "module_id": "M3_matched_protection",
+      "purpose_oneline": "Use `C_r` and local discrepancy to form matched protection schedules while keeping budget meanings separate.",
+      "step_ids": ["S4"]
+    },
+    {
+      "module_id": "M4_validation",
+      "purpose_oneline": "Test contact-transition divergence and bounded transfer with permutation and oracle controls.",
+      "step_ids": ["S5"]
+    }
+  ],
+  "plain_method_modules_zh": [
+    {
+      "module_id": "M1_background",
+      "purpose_oneline": "提供可 replay 的 calibration state，并固定 paired measurement 所需的 exact version 与 configuration boundary。",
+      "step_ids": ["S1"]
+    },
+    {
+      "module_id": "M2_one_transition_proxy",
+      "purpose_oneline": "建立有界的 single-site W/A intervention，并计算 one-control-transition `C_r` signal。",
+      "step_ids": ["S2", "S3"]
+    },
+    {
+      "module_id": "M3_matched_protection",
+      "purpose_oneline": "使用 `C_r` 和 local discrepancy 形成 matched protection schedule，同时分开表达不同 budget 的含义。",
+      "step_ids": ["S4"]
+    },
+    {
+      "module_id": "M4_validation",
+      "purpose_oneline": "通过 permutation 和 oracle controls 检验 contact-transition divergence 与有界 transfer。",
+      "step_ids": ["S5"]
+    }
+  ]
+}

