+      "step_id": "S1",
+      "what_to_do": "Before any paired measurement, freeze the calibration registry and pre-run manifest, including the exact Fast-WAM checkpoint identity and the `idm` configuration. Make controller, RNG, history, and cache restoration executable so the calibration state can be replayed. For the Optional IDM path, halt if the exact checkpoint identity is absent or mismatched.",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "Both branches are interpretable as a paired consequence only when they start from the same recoverable state. This preserves the version boundary instead of treating an unverified checkpoint as interchangeable."
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S2",
+      "what_to_do": "For each numerical weight or activation site r, apply the chosen low-bit operator only at r and keep every other target site at FP16. Produce the single-site low-bit branch paired with the FP16 reference for the same calibration record.",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "This isolates the bounded single-site intervention and avoids treating joint coupling, joint-low-bit marginal effects, or joint optimality as new claims."
+    },
+    {
+      "step_id": "S3",
+      "what_to_do": "Run both branches to produce the full action chunk. From the restored state, execute only the first action and record the next observation. Compute `C_r` from normalized full-action-chunk MSE plus next-observation pixel L1, alongside the local score.",
+      "why_this_makes_sense": "This defines a one-control-transition proxy for action-mediated consequence. `C_r` is not task loss, a full-horizon/replan marginal, or a jointly-low-bit marginal."
